Leetcode-704.-Binary-Search
Description
Given an array of integers nums which is sorted in ascending order, and an integer target, write a function to search target in nums. If target exists, then return its index. Otherwise, return -1.

You must write an algorithm with O(log n) runtime complexity.

Solution
Binary search:

A searching algorithm in which operates on a sorted array . Instead of checking every element one by one like in linear search, it repeatedly divides the search space into two halves until the target element is found or the search space becomes empty.

If nums[mid] == target, then we have found the element and return mid.

If nums[mid] < target, it means the target must lie in the right half, so we shift l = mid + 1.

If nums[mid] > target, it means the target must lie in the left half, so we shift r = mid - 1.

Algorithm
Initialise l as 0 and r as len(nums)-1.
Use while loop which loops until l<=r:
Calculate the mid value by adding l and r , and dividing it by 2.
Check if the target and mid value are equal and if they are then return the mid index.
Check if the target is less than mid value , if it is then decrement the r pointer as mid-1.
Else increment the l pointer as mid+1
Code
class Solution:

def search(self, nums: List[int], target: int) -> int:
    l=0
    r=len(nums)-1

    while l<=r:
        mid=(l+r)//2
        if nums[mid]<target:
            l=mid+1
        elif nums[mid]==target:
            return mid
        else:
            r=mid-1
    return -1
Complexity
Time Complexity :

O(log n) (because the array size is divided by 2 at each step).

Space Complexity :

O(1) (we only use a few variables, no extra space).
